// A panic reached through RECURSION, so the same function name appears in the
// backtrace several times at three different call rows.
//
// arrays_index_panic_call_chain already walks four frames, but every one of
// them is a different function, which a walker that keyed frames by function
// - or that suppressed a repeat as a cycle - would still print correctly.
// Recursion is the shape that tells those apart: the frames must all be there,
// in order, and the two recursive rows must name the CALL site inside `down`
// while the innermost row names the index expression.
fn down(a: int[], n: int) -> int {
    if n == 0 {
        return a[9];
    }
    return down(a, n - 1);
}

@entrypoint
fn main() -> int {
    let xs: int[] = [1, 2, 3];
    return down(xs, 2);
}
